<task id="configuring_search_criteria_290afd" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Configuring Search Criteria</title>
   <shortdesc>You can configure additional fields to be available for search functionality during the check-in and</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">user-0266f</author>
      <critdates>
         <revised modified="Nov 25, 2018"/>
      </critdates>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Field</keyword>
        <keyword>Search</keyword>
        <keyword>Criteria</keyword>
        <keyword>fields</keyword>
        <keyword>check</keyword>
        <keyword>object</keyword>
        <indexterm>Field</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Search</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Criteria</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p>You can configure additional fields to be available for search functionality during the check-in and check-out process. </p>
         <fig>
            <title>98672814</title>
            <image href="../attachments/98672805/98672814.png" width="737" height="461" placement="break">
               <alt>placeholder</alt>
            </image>
         </fig>
         <p>To configure Search Criteria, </p>
      </context>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>For an object, create a fieldset in your Salesforce Org. For example, to configure search criteria for Account object, you need to create a fieldset on the Account object. </cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>To create a fieldset, navigate to your Salesforce object and click Field Set from the right-hand side setup menu.
Enter the following values for the Field Set Label and Field Set Name:</cmd>
            <info>
               <table>
                  <tgroup cols="2">
                     <colspec colname="c1"/>
                     <colspec colname="c2"/>
                     <thead>
                        <row>
                           <entry>
                              <p>Field</p>
                           </entry>
                           <entry>
                              <p>Value</p>
                           </entry>
                        </row>
                     </thead>
                     <tbody>
                        <row>
                           <entry>
                              <p>Field Set Label</p>
                           </entry>
                           <entry>
                              <p>ChatterSearchCriteriaFieldSet</p>
                           </entry>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                           <entry>
                              <p>Field Set Name</p>
                           </entry>
                           <entry>
                              <p>ChatterSearchCriteriaFieldSet</p>
                           </entry>
                        </row>
                     </tbody>
                  </tgroup>
               </table>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click Save.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Drag and drop your required fields in the fieldset area. </cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click Save. </cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
      <result>
         <p>The fields are now available as part of the search criteria during the check-in and check-out process, </p>
         <p>Configuring Search Criteria functionality does not support the following data types of Salesforce fields:</p>
         <ul>
            <li>Rich Text Area</li>
            <li>Phone</li>
         </ul>
      </result>
   </taskbody>
</task>